Package: uzunyx-grub
Version: @VERSION@
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: emi <285864120+antarest47@users.noreply.github.com>
Pre-Depends: grub2-common
Depends: grub2-common
Description: Uzunyx GRUB theme and hidden boot menu
 A neutral, dark GRUB theme for Uzunyx (the boot splash's #111318
 background, a centred menu without icons, the chosen entry framed like
 Uzunyx windows), replacing Debian's blue picture, and a hidden boot menu
 like Ubuntu's or Linux Mint's: GRUB waits one second and boots, and Esc
 (or F4, or holding Shift) shows the menu. If os-prober is enabled (there
 are other systems to choose from) the menu shows as usual.
 .
 It also keeps GRUB from printing "Loading Linux ..." and "Loading initial
 ramdisk ..." before the boot splash: /etc/grub.d/10_linux is diverted and
 replaced by a copy with quiet_boot="1", made again whenever grub2-common
 updates it.
